# Normalise line endings to LF inside the repository, whatever the machine.
# This project is written on Windows, will be built by CI on Linux, and will
# eventually be built on macOS for iOS. Without this, the same file looks
# changed on every machine and diffs become unreadable.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending converted — doing so corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
*.vault binary

# His feedback documents, added 28 August 2026 when `Thought Process/` stopped
# being ignored. `* text=auto eol=lf` above applies to everything, and while
# Git's own heuristic would almost certainly classify both of these as binary
# on content, "almost certainly" is not a good basis for the only copy of a
# document that exists nowhere else. A `.docx` is a zip archive and a `.pdf`
# has binary streams in it; one rewritten CRLF in either is a file that no
# longer opens.
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
